<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/67f600a06ec7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4412] Of the 1,533 U.S. and U.K. finance professionals polled by Medius, 85% viewed such scams as an \"existential\" threat to their organization's financial security." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4412" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6b926f248753> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4411] Experts predict that generative AI could enable fraud losses to reach $40 billion in the United States by 2027, growing at a compound annual rate of 32%." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/709ab1573ced> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "KYC is a financial service standard requiring banks to verify customers' identities, risk profiles and financial records." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4836" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/72be7bd114f2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "We're seeing everything from deepfake CEOs asking for wire transfers to scammers using cloned voices to fool Bank customer service agents." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8d2daaeeedfc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[4412] In May, British engineering group Arup was in the spotlight after reports that scammers successfully siphoned $25 million from the company by using deepfake technology to pose as the organization's CFO." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4412" .

