    airo:evidenceText "With AI-generated passports, deepfakes and websites, fraudsters are running sophisticated, large-scale, ultra-realistic scams." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7bf4e40869fe> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Banks are actively exploring solutions to the problem, from cutting-edge behavioral analysis to experimenting blockchain verification." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a3f5d54b9ffb> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Banks are exploring the use of biometrics, blockchain, and machine learning to enhance security and protect their customers' assets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a854b57610fc> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Many people on social media have pointed out how easy it is to now create fake passport images using ChatGPT's latest image generation capabilities, one of the most widely used AI tools." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ea0a4399b245> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Advanced language generation and rapid processing enable mass email generation, domain spoofing and content personalization." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4836" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0711634a903b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 2024, United Kingdom-based Arup --- an engineering consulting firm --- lost around $25 million after fraudsters tricked a staff member into transferring funds during a live video conference." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4836" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/09e59049314b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In another example, the Guardian reported in May that advertising group WPP had been the target of an unsuccessful deepfake scam." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4412" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/27eee322ad71> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "\"Digital services, tied to faster and more efficient payment systems, enable criminals to move stolen money out of the system and across country borders at speed,\" says Jason Lane-Sellers, director of Fraud & Identity at LexisNexis Risk Solutions." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/29677f7cc76c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Generative AI could enable fraud losses to reach $40 billion in the U.S. by 2027, Big Four accounting firm Deloitte said in a May report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4412" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/47ef093b4dfd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A California financial regulator on Wednesday slapped five purported financial services companies with cease-and-desist orders." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6516" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/71a596046722> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "According to the Federal Trade Commission, consumers reported losing more than $10 billion to fraud in 2023, marking a 14% increase from the previous year." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7c46be76d9f0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In the 5-page order issued by the California Department of Financial Protection and Innovation (DFPI) that details allegations of the sale of unauthorized securities, the agency claims that \"Michael Vanes\" was presented as CEO of Maxpread Technologies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "6516" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/9add3b4100e8> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "However, they were unknowingly depositing funds into a JPMorgan Chase account." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4836" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a22f917520ce> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Of the 1,533 U.S. and U.K. finance professionals polled by Medius, 85% viewed such scams as an \"existential\" threat to their organization's financial security." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4412" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a742d13c8c7a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In May, British engineering group Arup was in the spotlight after reports that scammers successfully siphoned $25 million from the company by using deepfake technology to pose as the organization's CFO." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4412" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/e9decba7765b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 1 such case, scammers opened a JPMorgan Chase bank account and scammed at least one victim in the United States through a clone of Exante." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b20562e0758a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC), the North American Securities Administrators Association (NASAA), and the Financial Industry Regulatory Authority (FINRA) also issued a joint warning about a rise in investment frauds involving AI and other new technologies." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/83dc894202cf> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The investigation also found that one of the fake crypto-trading websites used by the scammers was AdmiralsFX, which copied the branding of Admirals, a real forex and CFDs broker." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b404ce0ffeba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Experts predict that generative AI could enable fraud losses to reach $40 billion in the United States by 2027, growing at a compound annual rate of 32%." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4411" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/738ab81d7986> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Exante did not report the incident to JPMorgan Chase as they do not have a presence in the US and does not bank with JP Morgan in anyway." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4818" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a8d28b93469c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Deepfakes use generator and discriminator algorithms to create a digital duplicate and evaluate realism, enabling them to convincingly mimic someone's facial features and voice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4836" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f7049e38d6ba> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "In 1 such case, scammers cloned the Exante platform." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "4836" .

